{"name":"Hit the Hay","hex":"#efc872","fetched":"2026-10-12","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"hit the hay","whole":true,"parts":[{"part":"Verb","definitions":["To go to bed."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/hit_the_hay"}],"entries":[{"title":"Hit the Hay","blocks":[{"text":"Hit the Hay is a 1945 American musical comedy film directed by Del Lord and starring Judy Canova, Ross Hunter, Fortunio Bonanova and Doris Merrick. It was produced and distributed by Columbia Pictures."}],"image":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/en/0/08/Hit_the_Hay.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail_unscaled","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Hit_the_Hay","wikidata":"Q60792351"},{"title":"Sleep","blocks":[{"text":"Sleep is a state of reduced mental and physical activity in which consciousness is altered and certain sensory activity is inhibited. During sleep, there is a marked decrease in muscle activity and interactions with the surrounding environment. While sleep differs from wakefulness in terms of the ability to react to stimuli, it still involves active brain patterns, making it more reactive than a coma or disorders of consciousness."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/1/18/Domenico_Fetti_-_Sleeping_Girl_-_WGA7863.jpg/330px-Domenico_Fetti_-_Sleeping_Girl_-_WGA7863.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Sleep","wikidata":"Q35831"},{"title":"Hay","blocks":[{"text":"Hay is grass, legumes, or other herbaceous plants that have been cut and dried to be stored for use as animal fodder, either for large grazing animals raised as livestock, such as cattle, horses, goats, and sheep, or for smaller domesticated animals such as rabbits and guinea pigs. Pigs can eat hay, but they do not digest it as efficiently as herbivores do."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/4/4c/Roundbale1.jpg/330px-Roundbale1.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Hay","wikidata":"Q336989"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/7/7d/1900_The_Awakening.jpg/500px-1900_The_Awakening.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/7/7d/1900_The_Awakening.jpg/500px-1900_The_Awakening.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"\"The Awakening\", an illustration to writing by Leo Tolstoy","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3A1900_The_Awakening.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/3/33/Pillow_Height_in_Side-Lying_Position.png/250px-Pillow_Height_in_Side-Lying_Position.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/3/33/Pillow_Height_in_Side-Lying_Position.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail_unscaled 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/3/33/Pillow_Height_in_Side-Lying_Position.png/250px-Pillow_Height_in_Side-Lying_Position.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":" Pillow height during side sleeping affects the spine and neck muscles. See Sleep and musculoskeletal health.","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3APillow_Height_in_Side-Lying_Position.png"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/7/79/Noon%2C_rest_from_work_-_Van_Gogh.jpeg/500px-Noon%2C_rest_from_work_-_Van_Gogh.jpeg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/7/79/Noon%2C_rest_from_work_-_Van_Gogh.jpeg/1280px-Noon%2C_rest_from_work_-_Van_Gogh.jpeg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/7/79/Noon%2C_res